# t15-tui: what is left of the nr-tui-* fragments for the lead (hot files and other owners' crates)

Everything that was an edit inside mixdog-tui, mixdog-tui-widgets, mixdog-term and mixdog-repl is applied (their Cargo.toml edges
and features, the dev-dependencies, the module lines, the three recorder MODULES lines of
mixdog-tui-widgets/tests/recorders/record-ink-frames.mjs, and the removal of the private copies of
`is_live_spinner_meta_visible` / `completed_tail_appended_this_commit` in mixdog-tui/src/surface/layout in favour of
mixdog_tui_widgets::spinner). The original fragments nr-tui-app-run, -slash, -surface-layout, -widgets-panels, -term-os, -editor,
-mouse, -repl, -view, -footer, -panels and -pickers-{extensions,model,settings} are deleted.

## native/core/Cargo.toml, native/core/Cargo.lock

Already in the tree: members `crates/mixdog-repl`, `crates/mixdog-tui`, workspace dependencies `mixdog-repl`, `mixdog-tui`, and the
lock entries of `mixdog-tui` (incl. dev-dependencies portable-pty, vte, tempfile, mixdog-cli, mixdog-core) and `mixdog-repl`.
`cargo nextest run -p mixdog-tui --locked` accepts the lock as it is (no regeneration needed for these two packages).

## native/core/crates/mixdog-workspace-hack/Cargo.toml

Run the workspace-hack refresh once for the new members `mixdog-tui` and `mixdog-repl` (both Cargo.toml files already carry the
`mixdog-workspace-hack` edge). The two crates take no external dependency that is not already in the lock.

## native/core/crates/mixdog-cli main.rs / the entry (nr-tui-entry-argv, nr-tui-switch)

* `--plain`: `mixdog_repl::run(mixdog_repl::ReplOptions { provider, model, tool_mode, cwd }, Arc<dyn mixdog_repl::Footer>)`; the footer is
  `Arc::new(mixdog_tui::footer::StatuslineRenderer)` built as the footer fragment describes; exit code 0 / 130 / 1; the process
  lifecycle ledger brackets the call; `--help` is the entry's argv handling.
* the terminal UI: `mixdog_tui::run::run_tui(TuiOptions { .., tool_mode, remote, force_onboarding, worktree, resume })`.

## compose*.rs / protocol tables

No row, no SERVICE_PENDING change from any of these fragments.

## For other owners (not hot, not in my crates)

* mixdog-core-domains route_set_service.rs: accept `validateOnly` in the `route/set` selection (add it to `OPTION_KEYS`, pass it as
  `SetRouteOptions.validate_only`) so `/model <name>` of the plain REPL can validate before it compacts (Node order).
* mixdog-app-server-daemon statusline_port.rs reads `settings.json` / `cc-statusline-last.json` from `CLAUDE_CONFIG_DIR` / `~/.claude`;
  Node reads them from `MIXDOG_CONFIG_DIR` (default `~/.mixdog`), as the footer here does.
* `getSettingsSnapshot` has no `voice: { enabled }` member (the settings row costs one extra `getVoiceStatus` call); the application's
  `AppCtx::store_call` must add the session `threadId` to `toggleVoice` or the install runs without visible progress.
* `mixdog-session-view` does not export the router's table of targets: `AppStore::has_method` answers true for every name
  (a missing method answers with its own `Err` instead of Node's silent `null`); exporting `has_action(name)` restores it.
